{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Three years it shall be to you arelim.</b> The expression ערלה is an expression of covering, as though the fruits are covered in the trees, so that one has no permission to touch them or to enjoy them." "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense (peshat), the reason of the commandment is to give honor to the Holy One, blessed be He, from the first fully ripened fruit, the choicest of our land, and that we not eat of it until we bring one year's worth of all its fruit for rejoicing. And it is known that a tree within three years produces little fruit and it has no taste or fragrance, and therefore it is not fitting that we offer it before HaShem; and most trees do not produce fruit until the fourth year, because their strength is not completed within three, until the fourth year arrives. And so it is in the nature of generation in the human species itself, which is what they said concerning a woman less than three years and one day old: it is like putting a finger in the eye, and her virginity returns. And they required one day corresponding to the fourth year, when the fruit is consecrated. And therefore this commandment came: that we not taste from the sapling we planted until we bring all its first ripe fruit, the fit and the choice — holy, for rejoicing, to HaShem — to eat it there and to praise His name upon it." "<b>And from the way of</b> nature, further: the fruit within three years is very harmful to the body, because it contains moistures drawn from the power of the earth's suckling, and not enough time has yet passed over it for it to be heated by the power of the sun and heated by the power of the air. And therefore the entire fruit — its earthy and watery aspects — the moisture overpowers it greatly, and eating it is harmful, like the case of a fish that has no scales, upon which moisture overpowers it all the more, because of the abundance of the moistures of the waters in which it dwells, in their lower depths and in their deep places." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> 'Three years it shall be to you arelim' speaks of an infant who cannot yet speak fluently, and 'in the fourth year, holy' — for his father consecrates him to Torah, 'for rejoicing to HaShem,' which means he praises the Holy One, blessed be He, and 'in the fifth year you shall eat' — for he begins to read in Torah. From here onward, to add for you from here onward, our Rabbis of blessed memory taught: 'A five-year-old for Scripture, a ten-year-old for Mishnah.' For in this world an Israelite begets and leads his son to the schoolhouse to engage in Torah, and through his sin he dies and does not enjoy him. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to them: In this world, because the evil inclination is present among you, you sin and your children die; but in the world to come, I will remove the evil inclination from you, and you will beget and rejoice in them, as it is said (Isaiah 65:23): ״לא יגעו לריק ולא ילדו לבהלה כי זרע ברוכי ה' המה וצאצאיהם אתם.״" "<b>By way of reason (sekhel):</b> In the reason of this commandment — heaven and earth are the cause for the bringing forth of fruit by the supernal power, and they correspond, in likeness, to male and female: this one acts and this one receives. And this is the matter of what is written concerning the rain that comes from heaven, as it is said (Isaiah 55:10): ״והולידה והצמיחה״. And until three years, the earth does not concur in the ripening of the fruit, nor do the heavens concur to grant it the power of ripening. Since this is so, whoever eats of the fruit within three years — lo, this is as though he shows that he has no portion in heaven and earth, and no portion in the Holy One, blessed be He; behold, he takes it without permission from above and from below. Therefore the Torah forbade it within three. And our Master Moses, of blessed memory, gave a reason for this commandment in chapter seven of the Guide of the Perplexed: that the idolaters in those times had kinds of sorcery that they practiced at the time of planting trees, and each one of them had ready at hand something they would scatter there at the time of planting, at the place of the tree or around it, and they thought that the tree would hasten to produce its fruit faster than what is accustomed by the nature of the world. And therefore the Torah commanded the prohibition of the fruit that comes before three years, so that they not come to do those evil deeds, for most trees bring forth fruit in the fourth year. And the command that we eat it before HaShem is the opposite of their eating it before idols, for the disease of the soul, which is false belief in the imagination, is not cured except by its opposite." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the commandment of orlah — the Torah distanced the planting for three years corresponding to the three upper first ones concerning which we have no apprehension, and corresponding to them as well תהו ובהו וחשך (unformed and void and darkness); and the fourth year corresponds as well to ורוח אלהים מרחפת על פני המים, for it is not complete concealment and not complete apprehension — so too the fourth year is not a complete permit, for it is permitted through redemption and forbidden without redemption; and the fifth year corresponds to the ה׳ of יהי אור, which is complete form, for so the fifth year is a complete permit, and this is ״להוסיף לכם תבואתה״ — with the addition of the ה׳, for so the אור (light) is mentioned five times in the passage; and therefore Scripture mentions here three times ערלה, as it says ״וערלתם ערלתו יהיה לכם ערלים״, to allude that each and every year has its own matter, which is its likeness, and all three of them are complete concealment. And this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {5 "The lemma and method-header are fused in the source; read as ועל דרך הקבלה. The word כגנד appears to be a typographical error for כנגד ('corresponding to'); rendered accordingly. The three-fold repetition of ערלה in the cited verse is the traditional counting of the word's three occurrences within וערלתם ערלתו שלש שנים יהיה לכם ערלים."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:19.639179778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}